  "source": "pubchem",
  "note": "Los Alamos dates Mosander's separation to 1842. The later 'erbia' turned out to be a mixture of the oxides of five elements: erbium, scandium, holmium, thulium and ytterbium. Klemm and Bommer made fairly pure metal by reducing the chloride with potassium vapour.",
